Good morning, 

This parcel has been roughly in its current configuration since 1992 with DB1794-855 (attached) with slight shifts to the eastern boundary line due to creek movement over the years. Prior to the 1992 deed, it appears the lands were owned by Key Homes Inc / Equitable Construction Co which owned many parcels in Durham. The parcel also shares the SW boundary with Durham Public Schools whose deeds are hard to track. As such, I would recommend contacting a real estate attorney to do a title search on this parcel.

I will forward your request to our collections department to answer question #4 regarding back taxes, tax liens, or special assessments.

Thank you,

MARGARET VANDERFORD |GIS CARTOGRAPHER

Pronouns: she/her/hers

201 East Main Street, 3rd floor 
Durham, North Carolina 27701

Office (919) 560-0390 | Fax (919) 328-6180

mvanderford@dconc.gov

Re: 1621 Clermont Rd, Durham NC, 27713 - PIN 0728808242 / REID 153775 (9.4
acres).

Hello,
I'm doing due diligence on a possible purchase. Durham Planning referred me
to you for the questions below. A quick reply, even partial, would help me
a lot.

1. The recorded plat (PB 127, 25.pdf attached) appears to cover 1621 + 1615
Clermont but not the SW/SE area your GIS shows in 1621 (1621-clermont.png).
Why the mismatch - was this tract divided or recombined? See the pdf and
png attached to see the discrepancy in the boundaries recorded.
2. Can you send the recorded plats and deeds showing the parcel's
division/recombination history?
3. What is the deed/plat recordation date for 1621? (Planning needs it to
set the impervious-surface limit under UDO 8.7.3B.)
4. Are there back taxes, tax liens, or special assessments on the parcel?

Thanks,
Kalin Ivanov

Ref:MSG1137323_PeF2u3UlnHmtMKzx77RQ
